telegram-desktop (7.2.5+ppa1~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 7.2.5, skipping the 7.2.6 pre-release.
  * The whole 7.2.x series concerns upstream's v2 update system — a rotated
    then revoked signing key, and finally a new autoupdate manifest source.
    None of it affects this package, which is built with
    DESKTOP_APP_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE=ON and is updated through the PPA instead.
  * Includes the 7.1.5 Linux crash fix ("Destroy main window on X11 on
    explicit hide only", bea90214ec). The 7.2 branch forked on 28 August,
    before 7.1.5 shipped on 2 September, so this was verified rather than
    assumed: the commit is an ancestor of v7.2.5.
  * No packaging changes. Only the lib_base submodule moved; cld3 still needs
    no protoc, the QSB_EXECUTABLE and GI_GIR_PATH workarounds still apply, the
    Qt 6.10 accessibility patch still applies, and the set of required
    external dependencies is unchanged.
  * The tg_owt, tde2e and rnnoise pins are unchanged.

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 13:36:20 +0000

telegram-desktop (7.1.4+ppa1~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 7.1.4: wider rich message bubbles for wide content,
    fitting quality selection for video autoplay in channels, gift messages
    disabled for recipients who charge for messages, and fixes for the call
    panel, profile info and chat list menu, self-destructing media appearing
    in previews and downloads, and re-encoding of edited videos.
  * No packaging changes. The release moves the lib_tl and lib_ui submodules;
    cld3 still needs no protoc, the QSB_EXECUTABLE and GI_GIR_PATH workarounds
    still apply, the Qt 6.10 accessibility patch still applies, and the set of
    required external dependencies is unchanged.
  * The tg_owt, tde2e and rnnoise pins are unchanged.

