telegram-desktop (7.1.1+ppa1~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 7.1.1.
  * Drop the protobuf CMake shim, along with the libprotobuf-dev and
    protobuf-compiler build dependencies. Upstream reworked
    cmake/external/cld3 to ship hand-written replacements for the three
    generated .pb.h headers instead of running protoc, and removed
    stage('protobuf') from Telegram/build/prepare/prepare.py, so the
    find_package(protobuf REQUIRED CONFIG) that the shim existed to satisfy is
    gone. Language detection still works: lib_spellcheck continues to link
    external_cld3.
  * No other packaging changes. The release moves 18 submodule pointers but
    adds no new external dependency, and the QSB_EXECUTABLE and GI_GIR_PATH
    workarounds plus the Qt 6.10 accessibility patch all still apply.
  * The tg_owt, tde2e and rnnoise pins are unchanged.

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 19:45:29 +0000

telegram-desktop (7.0.9+ppa1~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 7.0.9: saving rich messages to HTML and importing
    them back, a custom prompt tab in the article editor, an experimental
    Vulkan rendering option on Linux, and crash fixes.
  * No packaging changes needed. The release moves the codegen, lib_ui,
    lib_webview, MicroTeX and cmake_helpers submodules, but cmake_helpers
    changes nothing under external/cld3, external/glib or external/qt, so the
    protobuf CMake shim, QSB_EXECUTABLE and GI_GIR_PATH workarounds all still
    apply. The Vulkan option adds no new build dependency.
  * The tg_owt, tde2e and rnnoise commits pinned in
    Telegram/build/prepare/prepare.py are unchanged; the pins that moved
    (patches, dav1d, libavif) are used only by upstream's static build.

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 19:05:48 +0000

